{"id":"high-capitals","title":"Highest capital cities","prompt":"Name the 10 national capitals that sit highest above sea level","noun":"capital cities","category":"Geography","metric":"Elevation above sea level","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: List of capital cities by elevation","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_capital_cities_by_elevation","asOf":"2026-11-20"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"La Paz","aliases":["La Paz, Bolivia","Chuquiago","Lapaz","Chukuta","Nuestra Señora de La Paz","Administrative capital of Bolivia","Chukiyawu"],"value":"3,640 m","n":3640,"article":"La Paz","fact":{"text":"Bolivia's seat of government is the world's highest administrative capital, and has the largest urban cable car network in the world.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Paz"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Quito","aliases":["San Francisco de Quito","Quiteño","Capital of Ecuador","Quito, Ecuador","Keyto","Queeto","Qeeto","Qito","Quitoh","Santiago de Quito","City of Quito","Quito, Pichincha"],"value":"2,850 m","n":2850,"article":"Quito","fact":{"text":"Ecuador's capital sits on the slopes of an active volcano, Pichincha, and is the capital closest to the Equator, which crosses its northern suburbs.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quito"}},{"rank":3,"name":"Sucre","aliases":["Sucre, Bolivia","Constitutional capital of Bolivia","Chuquisaca","Sucer","Historic City of Sucre","Sucre, Oropeza"],"value":"2,790 m","n":2790,"article":"Sucre","fact":{"text":"Bolivia's constitution makes it the country's true capital; La Paz, higher still, is only the seat of government.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sucre"}},{"rank":4,"name":"Bogotá","aliases":["Santa Fe de Bogotá","Bogota D.C.","Bogotá, Colombia","Santafé de Bogotá","Santa Fé de Bacatá","Bogotá Capital District","Distrito Especial, Colombia","Bogotá, Special District","Capital of Colombia","Bogotá Distrito Capital","Distrito Capital de Bogotá","Bogota, Columbia","City of Bogotá","Santafé de Bogotá D.C.","Bogotano","Capital District, Colombia"],"value":"2,625 m","n":2625,"article":"Bogotá","fact":{"text":"Colombia's capital stands on a high Andean plateau, the Bogotá savanna, home to half a million Muisca people when the Spanish arrived.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bogot%C3%A1"}},{"rank":5,"name":"Addis Ababa","aliases":["Adis Abeba","Adis Ababa","Addis Abeba","Finfinne","Capital of Ethiopia","Addis Adaba","Addis Ababa, Ethiopia","Addis Abba, Ethiopia","Addis Abba","Addis Ababa, ET","Adis abeda","Addis Abbaba","Sheger","Addiss Ababa","Capital city of Ethiopia"],"value":"2,355 m","n":2355,"article":"Addis Ababa","fact":{"text":"Ethiopia's capital is the highest in Africa; its name means 'new flower'.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Addis_Ababa"}},{"rank":6,"name":"Thimphu","aliases":["Thimphu, Bhutan","Thimbu","Thimpu","Capital of Bhutan"],"value":"2,334 m","n":2334,"article":"Thimphu","fact":{"text":"Bhutan's capital, the highest in Asia, has no airport and no traffic lights: police direct the traffic by hand.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thimphu"}},{"rank":7,"name":"Asmara","aliases":["Asmera","Capital of Eritrea","Piccola Roma","Asmara, Eritrea","Asmarra"],"value":"2,325 m","n":2325,"article":"Asmara","fact":{"text":"Italian architects built Eritrea's capital high up for its cool climate; in 2017 it became the first modernist city listed whole by UNESCO.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asmara"}},{"rank":8,"name":"Sanaa","aliases":["Sanaá, Yemen","San'a","Sana, Yemen","Sana`a","Ṣan‘ā’","Sana'h","Sa’nna","Sanaa, YM","Amanat Al Asimah Governorate","Amanat Al Asimah","Sana Municipality","Amanat Al-Asemah","Sanaa Municipality"],"value":"2,250 m","n":2250,"article":"Sanaa","fact":{"text":"Yemen's capital lies between the highest mountains in Arabia; the stone tower houses of its old city rise up to 8 storeys.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanaa"}},{"rank":9,"name":"Mexico City","aliases":["Mexican Federal District